{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1491012-aberrant-powers-check-my-math","id":1491012,"title":"Aberrant Powers - Check My Math","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-22T10:50:42-07:00","id":1491012,"title":"Aberrant Powers - Check My Math","content":"<span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Okay, I'm actually trying to do Something With Aberrant and wanted to make sure I get powers, so I'm going to describe a power set for characters and see if I've got it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A telekinetic (like Jean Grey or the Great and Powerful Turtle)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Moving Stuff: Quantum Anima 3 (free tags: Grab, Might and Strike). The Might tag makes this the telekinetic version of Mega-Strength 1. If I wanted to lift even more stuff (without having to Max Out), I'd need to buy a second (or third) Might tag.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* A telekinetic force field: Quantum Anima</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* a wall of telekinetic force - Quantum Construct with the Invisible Tag</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Levitation - Flight (obviously)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A force absorber similar to Sebastian Shaw or Bishop except Physical Force becomes Strength, Radiant Energy becomes Speed:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Mega Strength 1 &amp; Mega Dex 1 (necessary for Mega Speed), Mega Speed</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Absorption (with the Broad Tag)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Boost: I was thinking it should be &quot;Extra Attribute (1), Restricted (-2 - can only boost Dex after absorbing Radiant and only Strength after absorbing kinetic)&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A person made of steel (like Colossus but they can't change back)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* various picks from the Tank Archetype</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Adaptation, Dense Flesh</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* They'd be at Transcendence 4 (Epidermal Shift)</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2222-rickjonzz","name":"RickJonzz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2222_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:27:08-07:00","id":1491019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1491012-aberrant-powers-check-my-math#post1491012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Okay, I'm actually trying to do Something With Aberrant and wanted to make sure I get powers, so I'm going to describe a power set for characters and see if I've got it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A telekinetic (like Jean Grey or the Great and Powerful Turtle)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I miss the Great and all Powerful Turtle. I really liked that character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27511-fanggrip","name":"FangGrip","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:43:40-07:00","id":1491025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1491012-aberrant-powers-check-my-math#post1491012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A telekinetic (like Jean Grey or the Great and Powerful Turtle)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Moving Stuff: Quantum Anima 3 (free tags: Grab, Might and Strike). The Might tag makes this the telekinetic version of Mega-Strength 1. If I wanted to lift even more stuff (without having to Max Out), I'd need to buy a second (or third) Might tag.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* A telekinetic force field: Quantum Anima</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* a wall of telekinetic force - Quantum Construct with the Invisible Tag</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Levitation - Flight (obviously)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You can make it all as a suit, with each power as a different Technique.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1491012-aberrant-powers-check-my-math#post1491012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A force absorber similar to Sebastian Shaw or Bishop except Physical Force becomes Strength, Radiant Energy becomes Speed:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Mega Strength 1 &amp; Mega Dex 1 (necessary for Mega Speed), Mega Speed</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Absorption (with the Broad Tag)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Boost: I was thinking it should be &quot;Extra Attribute (1), Restricted (-2 - can only boost Dex after absorbing Radiant and only Strength after absorbing kinetic)&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You can make Boost Strength and Boost Dex as two Techniques of the same power and add the restricted to each to work only when absorbing radiant or kinetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickJonzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1491012-aberrant-powers-check-my-math#post1491012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A person made of steel (like Colossus but they can't change back)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* various picks from the Tank Archetype</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* Adaptation, Dense Flesh</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">* They'd be at Transcendence 4 (Epidermal Shift)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! You dont need to add all that transcendence if you dont want to, you can add the Transformation and thats all. Unless you really want the extra XP and antisocial part of transcendence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:47:02-07:00","id":1491026,"title":"","content":"For the Colossus-like character, Density with the Non-Living tag is a good way to go. You'll probably want to bump up the duration or maybe take the Transformation which makes it always-on. I allow that in a game because being extra heavy does have consequences in everyday life.<br /> <br /> Hopefully for the telekinetic you're using the Technique tag. It'll make that power set a LOT more cost-friendly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T13:44:40-07:00","id":1491039,"title":"","content":"Thanks all.<br /> In no particular order -<br /> * Yeah, I knew that Power Suites will save me a lot of points but I wanted to make sure I understood the basics before I got into more complicated stuff.<br /> * I missed the part where you can just use low and mid level transformations to reduce the XP cost of nova trait. I thought you had to accrue Transcendence before taking the Transformations. That makes things much simpler. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2222-rickjonzz","name":"RickJonzz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2222_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T17:17:16-07:00","id":1491057,"title":"","content":"Wouldn\u2019t the Great and Powerful Turtle have, as a Transformation, \u2018Dumbo syndrome\u2019? Considering he psychologically needs his shell to even <i>use</i> his powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T18:42:27-07:00","id":1491066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1491012-aberrant-powers-check-my-math?p=1491057#post1491057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn\u2019t the Great and Powerful Turtle have, as a Transformation, \u2018Dumbo syndrome\u2019? Considering he psychologically needs his shell to even <i>use</i> his powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. He didn't need his &quot;shell&quot; at first, but he could also only move a few tons early in his career. He eventually reached the point where he could lift the battleship New Jersey for almost 30 seconds (and performed an even more impressive feat during the Rox War). That sounds to me like he bought more dots in both Quantum and in Quantum Anima, using the extra dots to gain free Might Tags. Power Loss could be a result of increasing Transcendence or just a result of buying a level of the Power with a -6 xp discount.<br /> <br /> Although do note that he eventually gets over this complete block, allowing him to move a few pounds of weight even without his &quot;shell&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 08-22-2022, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}